# Line endings, decided by the repo rather than by each clone's core.autocrlf.
#
# The source CSVs are checksummed: etl/extract.py --offline verifies each file
# against a recorded sha256, and CI runs it on a fresh checkout. Git's default
# text handling rewrites CRLF to LF in the blob, which silently changes the
# bytes and makes every checksum fail on Linux. Marking them -text keeps the
# vendor's bytes exact.
raw_data/*.csv  -text
optimization/data/**  binary

# Code and config normalise to LF everywhere, so a Windows working copy and a
# CI runner see identical files.
*.py   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
